            <div xml:id="d529-a12">

                <pb facs="0733" n="639" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg639"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 3 to inclosure 3 in No.
                        517.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commandant to Mr. Hyatt.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Marine and Office of the Captain of the Port of
                                Santiago de Cuba</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santiago de
                                Cuba</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1896-05-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 21,
                    1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">To the Consul of the United States of
                        North America:</hi></p>
                <p>Yesterday I received your attentive official letter dated the day previous
                    acknowledging receipt of the communication dated the 18th instant which I sent
                    you, notifying your honor of the resolution of his excellency the general
                    commandant of marine department of Habana in reference to the citizen of your
                    nation named Bert S. Skiller.</p>
                <p>I lament very much the detention that the said individual suffers, but it is not
                    in my power to better his situation, as that, as well as he who subscribes,
                    depends upon the mentioned superior authority, who governs the marine
                    jurisdiction of the Island, and to whom as I have had the honor to say to you
                    has been sent under date of yesterday the testimony asked for, which has to pass
                    the ordinary jurisdiction; I have transmitted to-day copy of your letter to said
                    superior authority.</p>
                <p>God keep you many years.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Manuel de Eliza.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
